1. e4 e5 2. Qh5 Nc6 { [%cal Gc6e5] } 3. Bc4 g6 4. Qf3 Nf6 5. d3 Nd4 { Centralising the knight and chasing the queen away } 6. Qe3?? (6. Qd1 Bg7 7. c3 Nc6 8. Nf3) 6... Nxc2+ 7. Ke2 Nxe3 8. Bxe3 d5 { Start opening up the centre to weakened the exposed king. (Converting material advantages) } 9. exd5 Nxd5 10. Nf3 { [%cal Gf3e5] } 10... Bg7 { [%cal Gg7e5] } 11. Nc3 Nxc3+ 12. bxc3 O-O 13. d4 exd4 14. cxd4 Re8!! { [%cal Ge8e2] } 15. Rhd1 Bg4 16. h3 Bxf3+ { Removing the defender of the d4 pawn. } 17. gxf3 Bxd4 18. Rab1 Qf6 { No need to get fixated on materials since black is up in material losing a pawn is not a big deal. } { [%csl Gb7][%cal Gb1b7] } 19. Rxd4 Qxd4 { [%cal Ge8e2] } 20. Rc1 Rad8 { Involve all pieces to ochrestrate an attack. } 21. Kf1 Rxe3!? { Sacrificing to simplify the position even more. } 22. fxe3 Qxe3 23. Re1 Qxf3+ 24. Kg1 Rd2 25. Re2 Rd1+ 26. Kh2 Rh1# *


