1. e4 e5 2. Bc4 Nf6 3. d4 { Plans to open up the centre immediately. } 3... exd4 4. e5 d5!? 5. exf6 (5. Bb5+ Nfd7 { [%cal Gc7c6,Gg1f3] }) (5. Bb3 Ne4 6. Qxd4 (6. f3 Qh4+ 7. g3 Nxg3 8. hxg3 Qxh1) 6... Be6) (5. exd6 Bxd6 6. Qxd4 Bb4+!! (6... O-O 7. Nh3 a6 8. O-O Bxh2+ 9. Kxh2 Qxd4) 7. c3 Qxd4!!) 5... dxc4 6. Qe2+ Be6 7. fxg7 Bxg7 8. Qh5 Nc6 9. Nf3 Qd7 { Prepare to castle queen side } (9... O-O { Castling kingside is very dangerous as the g7 pawn is no longer there and white can start threatening checkmate. } 10. Ng5) (9... Qe7? 10. O-O O-O-O 11. Bg5 (11. a4 Bd5 12. Re1) 11... f6) 10. Ng5 O-O-O 11. O-O Bd5 { Centralising } { [%cal Gd5h1] } 12. a4 Rdg8!? { x-ray white's king } { [%cal Gg8g1,Gd5h1] } 13. Nxf7 Bxf7 14. Qb5 Bd5 { Re-centralising the bishop to add more pressure on the g2 pawn } 15. a5 a6 { Prophylaxis move to prevent white from going a6 } 16. Qc5 (16. Qa4 Qh3!! 17. gxh3 Bf6+ 18. Bg5 Rxg5#) 16... Bf8 17. Na3 Rxg2+ (17... Bxc5 { Capturing the queen is good but...
"When you see a good move, look for a better one." }) 18. Kh1 Rg1+!! (18... Rxf2+ { Windmill technique } 19. Kg1 Rg2+ 20. Kh1 Rg4+ 21. Rf3 Bxf3#) 19. Kxg1 Qg4# *


