1. f3 e5 2. d3 d5 3. e4 Nf6 4. exd5 Nxd5 5. c4 Nf6 6. Bg5 (6. Be3 { Preventing black from playing bc5 } { [%csl Gc5][%cal Ge3c5] }) 6... Bc5! { Stop white from castling kingside in the long-term } 7. h4 Nc6 { Ignore white's terrible moves and continue developing } 8. Nc3 h6 { Either force bishop away or trade pieces to erased the pin-threat } 9. Bxf6 Qxf6 10. Nd5 { [%cal Gd5c7] } 10... Qd8 { Defend the c7 pawn } { [%cal Gd8c7,Gd5c7] } 11. Rb1 { Planning to advance pawn to b4 } { [%cal Gb2b4] } 11... a5 { Preventing b4 } 12. a3 { Try to reinforce b4 } { [%cal Gb2b4,Ga3b4] } 12... a4 { Preventing b4 again by en-passant } 13. b4 axb3 14. Rxb3 Nd4 { Improving the knight's position and also planning to advance the pawn to c6 to chase away the knight on d5 } 15. Rc3 c6 16. Ne3 Bxa3 17. g4 Bb4! { [%cal Gb4e1] } 18. Qb3 Nxb3 { White resign } *


