1. e4 e5 2. Nf3 Nc6 3. Bc4 d6? $14 { Obstruct the bishop from developing albeit black could still fianchetto his bishop at a cost of extra moves. } { [%cal Gf8d6] } 4. c3 { Prepare to control the centre } 4... Be6 (4... Bg4 5. Qb3 Bxf3 6. Bxf7+ Kd7 7. Qe6#) 5. Bxe6 { Ruining black's kingside pawn structure } 5... fxe6 6. d4 exd4 7. cxd4 e5 8. Nc3 (8. d5 { Generally closing the centre is a bad idea because it makes it harder for ourselves to attack the weakened king.
In this case, it is justify for us to close to centre because we have created a monster outpost on e6 for the knight. } 8... Nce7 9. Ng5 Nf6 10. Ne6 Qd7!! { Preventing Black from castling either side } { [%cal Ge6f8,Ge6d8] } 11. Nc3 c6 12. O-O cxd5 13. exd5 Nexd5 14. Nxd5 Nxd5 (14... Qxe6 15. Nc7+ { [%cal Gc7e8,Gc7e6,Gc7a8] }) 15. Qxd5) 8... exd4 9. Nxd4 Nxd4 10. Qxd4 Nf6 (10... c5 { Weakened the d5 square. It will be a great outpost for white's knight } { [%csl Gd5] } 11. Qc4 Nf6 12. Bg5 Be7 { Remove the defender of d5 square } 13. Bxf6 Bxf6 14. Nd5) 11. O-O Ng4 12. Bf4 { [%csl Gh4][%cal Gf4h2,Gd8h4,Gh4h2] } 12... g5 13. Qxh8 gxf4 14. Qxh7 Qf6 15. Qh5+ { Black resign } { [%cal Gh5e8,Gh5g4] } *


