1. d4 g5 2. Bxg5 f6 (2... Bg7 3. c3 c5 4. e3) 3. e4 h5 (3... fxg5 4. Qh5# { [%cal Gh5e8] }) 4. Be2 e5 (4... fxg5 5. Bxh5+ Rxh5 6. Qxh5#) 5. Bxh5+ Ke7 6. Be3 d6 7. Nc3 c6 8. Be2 { The bishop has already done it's job, white drop it back to allow further development. } 8... Bh6 9. Bxh6 Nxh6 10. Nf3 Ng4 11. Qd2 Na6 12. h3 { Forcing the knight away to remove the threat on the f2 pawn which allows the white to castle queen side } 12... Nh6 (12... Nc7 { [%cal Gh3g4,Gh8h1] } 13. Rg1 { Remove the pin threat and potentially supervise a pawn storm in the long term. } { [%cal Gg2g4,Gg4g5] } 13... Nh6 14. O-O-O) 13. O-O-O { Castle queen side to prevent black from starting an attack on king side. } { [%cal Gh8h3,Gd8g8,Gc8h3,Gg8g2] } 13... Nb4 14. a3 Na6 15. dxe5 fxe5?? { Weakened the g5 square which allows a devastating tactic as the rook is x-raying black's queen and white can give a check on the g5 square. } { [%cal Gd2g5,Gd1d8] } 16. Nxe5 dxe5 17. Qg5+ Ke8 18. Bh5+ Nf7 19. Rxd8# *


