1. e4 e5 2. Nf3 Nc6 3. d4 exd4 4. Nxd4 Bc5 5. Nxc6 bxc6 { Avoid going into the end game and potentially utilize the b file to attack white's queen side in the long run } 6. Nc3 d6 { Prepare to play nf6 } { [%cal Gd6e5,Gg8f6,Ge4e5] } 7. Bc4 Nf6 8. Bg5 h6 9. Bxf6? (9. Bh4 { [%cal Gh4d8] } 9... O-O 10. O-O Qe7 { To later get rid of the pin } { [%cal Ge7e5] }) 9... Qxf6 10. O-O (10. Qd2 Rb8 { [%cal Gb8b2] } 11. b3?? (11. Bb3) 11... Bb4) 10... O-O 11. b3?? Qxc3 12. Re1 Be6! 13. Re3 (13. Bxe6 fxe6 { [%cal Gf8f2,Gc5f2] } 14. Re2 Rxf2 15. Rxf2 Rf8 16. Qf1 Rxf2 17. Qxf2 Qxa1#) (13. Bd3 f5 { To open up the f file }) 13... Bxe3 { White resign } *


