1. d4 d5 2. a3 Nf6 3. Nf3 Bf5 4. Nc3 e6 5. Ne5 Bd6 6. Nxf7?! { White has no pieces to exploit the slight weakness of the king } (6. e3 O-O 7. Be2 c5 { Undermine the d4 square which is defending the knight on e5 } 8. O-O Nbd7 { [%cal Gd7e5] } 9. Nxd7 Nxd7 { [%cal Gd8h4,Ga8c8,Gc8c1,Gc5d4] }) 6... Kxf7 7. Bg5 h6 { Probing what white wants to do with his bishop. } 8. Bxf6 Qxf6 9. e3 Rf8 { Pseudo castling } 10. Nb5 Kg8 11. Nxd6 cxd6 12. Bb5 Qg6! { *Key moment } { [%cal Gg6g2] } (12... Be4 13. O-O Qg6 14. f3) (12... Bxc2?? 13. Qxc2 { [%cal Gf6f2,Gc2f2] }) (12... Bh3 13. O-O Qg6) (12... Bd3 13. Qxd3 Qxf2+ 14. Kd1 Qxg2) 13. O-O Bh3 14. Qf3 (14. g3 Bxf1 15. Bxf1) 14... Rxf3 15. Bd7 Qxg2# *


