1. e4 e5 2. Nf3 d6?! { Perhaps not a mistake but it's a poor move as:
1. Has not develop a piece.
2. Obstruct dark-square bishop from developing.
Both of these has serious concession. } 3. d4 { To exploit the serious concession white opens up the centre } 3... exd4 $14 4. Nxd4 Nc6 5. Nc3 Nxd4 6. Qxd4 Bd7 7. Bc4 Ne7 8. O-O Nc6 9. Qd1 (9. Qd5 Be6 10. Qd1 Bxc4) (9. Qd3 Ne5 { [%cal Ge5c4,Ge5d3] }) 9... Be7 10. Nd5 { Centralising and improving the knight's position } { [%cal Gc7c6] } 10... O-O 11. f4 { Increasing central control } 11... Be6 12. Bd2 { Prepare to transfer the bishop to c3 looking at the beautiful diagonal towards black's king } { [%cal Gd2c3,Gc3g7] } 12... Na5?? 13. Bxa5 b6 14. Bc3 c6 15. Qd4!? cxd5?? 16. Qxg7# *


