1. e4 e6 2. d4 d5 3. e5 f6? { Black should be attacking the base rather than the tip of the pawn chain.
(Note: What happen in most of the case when you attack the tip of the pawn chain - the opposing pawn (tip) can capture the attacking pawn which create/leaves behind an outpost to utilize later on) } (3... c5 4. c3 { [%cal Gc5d4,Gc3d4] }) 4. exf6 { Capturing to create a great outpost on e5 to later occupy with a piece } { [%csl Ge5] } 4... Nxf6 5. Nf3 Bd6 6. Bd3 (6. Ne5 { There's no need to rush to occupy the e5 square, it's just a square that is available to white in the future at a specific point } 6... Bxe5 7. dxe5) 6... Nbd7? { Obstruct the bishop from defending e6 } { [%cal Gc8e6] } 7. O-O b6 8. Re1 { [%cal Ge1e8] } 8... Nf8 9. Bg5 { Preparing to manoeuvre bishop to g3 to trade off black's bishop which is controlling the e5 outpost } { [%csl Ge5][%cal Gg5h4,Gh4g3,Gf3e5] } 9... Bd7 10. Bh4 Be7 11. Ne5 Ng6 { Looking to trade white's powerful knight } 12. Bxg6+ hxg6 13. Qd3 { Looking to potentially checkmate on f7 } { [%cal Gd3g6,Gg6f7] } 13... Rxh4 (13... Rh6 14. Bg5 { [%cal Gg5h6] }) 14. Qxg6+ Kf8 15. Qf7# *


