1. e4 c5 2. Bc4 Nc6 3. Nf3 e6 { Blunt white's light square bishop and prepare for d5 with tempo } { [%cal Gc4e6] } 4. d4 { Playing it open sicilian } 4... cxd4 5. Nxd4 Nf6 6. Nxc6 bxc6 7. e5? Qa5+ { [%cal Ga5e1,Ga5e5] } 8. Bd2 Qxe5+ 9. Be2 Qxb2 10. Nc3 Bb4 { Developed with tempo.
Although it would had been better to retreat the queen. If not the queen can turn into a liability where black will have to respond to all of the white's threat on the queen } (10... Qb6) 11. Rb1 Qa3 { [%cal Gb1b4,Ga3b4,Gc3d5,Gd2b4,Gd5b4] } 12. Rb3 (12. Rxb4 Qxb4 13. Nb5 { [%cal Gd2b4,Ge2b5,Gb5c7,Gc7e8,Gc7a8] } 13... Qxd2+ 14. Qxd2 cxb5) 12... Qa5 { Need to be cautious about the x-ray (Possible discovery from white) } { [%cal Gd2a5] } 13. O-O O-O 14. a3 Be7 15. Ne4 Qc7 16. Nxf6+ Bxf6 17. Bb4 c5 (17... Re8 18. Bd6 { [%cal Gd1d6,Gd6f8,Gd6b8] } 18... Qd8) 18. Bc3 Bxc3 19. Rxc3 d5 { Continue to expand central control } 20. Rb3 Bb7 { [%cal Gb7h1,Gd5d4] } 21. Bf3 Bc6 22. Rb2 { [%cal Gb2b8] } 22... Rab8 23. Rxb8 Rxb8 24. c4 d4 25. Bxc6 Qxc6 26. Qc2 g6 { Make some space for the king to avoid future back-rank mate } 27. h3 e5 28. f4 { [%cal Gf4e5] } 28... e4 29. Re1 e3 30. Re2 Qd6 31. g3 d3 { [%cal Gd3e2,Gd3c2] } 32. Qd1 dxe2 { [%cal Ge2e1] } 33. Qxe2 Qd2 34. Kf1 Rb1+ 35. Qe1 Rxe1# *


