1. e4 c5 2. Nf3 Nc6 3. d4 d6? { Mistake - It allows white to expand the centre with a tempo kicking black's knight away.
In Open Sicilian you want to take d4 instead. } { [%cal Gc5d4] } 4. d5 Ne5 5. Nxe5 { Ruining black's pawn structure } 5... dxe5 6. Nd2 { Preparing to jump to f3 or c4 to add tension to the weak pawn on e5 } { [%csl Ge5][%cal Gd2f3,Gf3e5,Gd2c4,Gc4e5] } 6... Nf6 7. Bd3 e6 { [%cal Ge6d5] } 8. c4 { [%cal Gc4d5,Ge6d5] } 8... Be7 9. Nf3 O-O 10. Nxe5 Nd7 { Offering a trade of white's centralise knight } 11. Nf3 { Declining trade as white has a space advantage in addition to being up an extra pawn so trading will only benefit black by lightening the tension. } 11... e5 12. O-O Bd6 { Defending the e5-pawn so that the knight on d7 is not tie down to defending the pawn and can re-locate to not obstruct the light square bishop } 13. h3 Nf6 14. a3 { [%cal Gb2b4] } 14... Bd7 15. Bd2 Qc8 { [%cal Gd7h3] } 16. b4 b6 17. Rc1 { [%cal Gc1c8] } 17... Bxh3 18. gxh3 Qxh3 19. Re1 { Create an escape route for the king } { [%cal Gg1f1,Gf1e2] } 19... Ng4 { [%cal Gg4h2,Gf3h2] } 20. Bf1 Qh5 21. Bg2 f5 22. Rc3 { Prepare to add more defender towards the king side } { [%cal Gc3g3] } 22... Rf7 { Preparing to bring more attackers towards white's king side } { [%cal Ga8f8] } 23. Ng5 Rf6 (23... Qh2+ 24. Kf1 { [%cal Gg2h3] } 24... Raf8 25. Rh3) 24. Rh3 Qg6 25. Nxh7 Rf7 26. Ng5 Rf6 27. exf5 Rxf5 28. Qxg4 Raf8 29. Qh4 { Black resign } *


