1. e4 e5 2. Nf3 Nc6 3. Bb5 a6 4. Ba4 Nf6 5. d3 b5 { Removing the tension on black's knight } 6. Bb3 Bc5 7. O-O d6 8. c3 O-O 9. d4 Bb6 { Taking the pawn would result in white having more control of the centre } (9... exd4 10. cxd4 Bb6 11. Bg5 { [%cal Ge4e5,Gg5d8] }) 10. d5? { White close off the diagonal to his own bishop and opens the diagonal for black's bishop } { [%cal Gb3d5,Gb6f2] } (10. dxe5 dxe5 11. Qxd8 Rxd8) 10... Ne7 11. Nbd2 Ng6 12. Bc2 Nh5 { Preparing to push f5 to start opening up white's king side } { [%cal Gf7f5] } 13. h3 { This weakens white's position as black could perhaps use it to tear open the h-file or g-file } 13... Nhf4 { [%cal Gc8h3,Gf4h3] } 14. Nb3 Bxh3 { Black could even prepare a queen and bishop battery before sacrificing though it's too slow as it allows white to bring in more defender } (14... Bd7 15. Kh2 Qc8 16. Ng1 { [%cal Gg1h3,Gh2h3] }) (14... f5 15. exf5 Bxf5 16. Bxf5 Rxf5 { [%cal Gd8f6,Ga8f8] }) 15. Bxf4 Nxf4 { [%cal Gd8d7,Gd7h3] } 16. gxh3 Qd7 17. Nh2 Qxh3 18. Qf3 Qh6 19. Nc1 f5 { Offer a trade to open up the file to bring more pieces to the attack } 20. Ne2 (20. exf5 Rae8 21. a4 e4 22. Bxe4 Nh3+ 23. Kh1 Ng5 { [%cal Gg5f3,Gg5e4,Ge8e4] } 24. Qg2 Rxe4 { [%cal Ge4h4,Gh4h1] }) 20... fxe4 21. Bxe4?? { [%cal Gf8f3,Gf4h3] } (21. Qxe4 Nh3+ (21... Qg6+ 22. Qxg6 Nxe2+ { [%cal Gh7g6] }) 22. Kh1 (22. Kg2 Nxf2 23. Qxh7+ Qxh7 24. Bxh7+ Kxh7) 22... Nxf2+) 21... Nh3+ 22. Qxh3 Qxh3 23. Bg2 Qh4 24. Rae1 Rxf2 25. Rxf2 Qxf2+ 26. Kh1 Qxe1+ 27. Nf1 Qxe2 { White resign } *


