1. e4 c5 2. Nf3 Nc6 3. d4 cxd4 4. Nxd4 g6 5. Be3 Bg7 6. c3 { Not a great move - It takes away the natural development square off his knight } { [%cal Gb1c3] } 6... Nf6 7. f3 { White is pushing a bunch of pawns which is weakening his position.
(Note: This should alert black to open up the centre ASAP to exploit the weakening of white's position.) } 7... O-O { King safety is number one priority before rushing to open up the centre. } 8. Be2 d5 { With the idea of opening up the centre to exposed the weaknesses of white's position } 9. exd5 Nxd5 10. Bf2 Nf4 { Applying more pressure to white's position } 11. O-O Nxd4 { With the tactical fork idea to trade every piece on the d4 square. At the end of trade-fest black would be up a piece and a pawn. } { [%cal Gf4e2,Ge2g1,Ge2d4] } 12. Bxd4 Bxd4+ 13. Kh1 (13. cxd4 Qxd4+ 14. Qxd4 (14. Kh1 Qxb2 { [%cal Gb2e2,Gb2a1] }) 14... Nxe2+ { [%cal Ge2g1,Ge2d4] }) 13... Bb6 14. Qxd8 Rxd8 15. Bc4 Bf5 16. Na3 Rd2 { Infiltrate the second rank } 17. g3 Bh3 { [%cal Gb6g1,Gd2g2,Gh3g2] } 18. gxf4 Bg2# *


