1. e4 g6 2. d4 Bg7 3. Nc3 e6 4. h4 { This is a multipurpose pawn push:
1. It can support the bishop on g5.
2. It can also be use as a battering ramp to advance to h5 to threaten opening up the h-file or it can be use to advance to h6 } { [%cal Gh4h5,Gc1g5,Gh5g6,Gh7g6] } 4... h5 { Weakened the g5 square } { [%csl Gg5] } (4... d6 5. h5 Nd7 6. h6 Bf6 { [%cal Gg8f6] } (6... Bf8)) (4... h6 5. h5 g5 6. f4 gxf4 7. Bxf4 { [%cal Gd1g4,Gg4g7] }) 5. Bg5 { Utilize the outpost gifted by black } 5... Bf6 6. Bxf6 Qxf6 7. e5 { White is cementing his control of the dark square as black has tremendously weakened it by playing e6 and g6. } { [%csl Gg7,Ge7,Gg5][%cal Ge7e6,Gg7g6] } 7... Qe7 8. Bd3 { Continue development } 8... Nh6 9. Nf3 O-O 10. Qd2 { Develop with tempo and prepare to castle queen side } { [%cal Gd2h6] } 10... Kg7 11. Ne4 { Prepare to manoeuvre the knight to the beautiful outpost on f6 } { [%csl Gf6][%cal Ge4f6,Ge5f6] } 11... d6 12. Nf6? dxe5 13. dxe5 Nd7 { Offering a trade to remove white's knight from occupying such a strong outpost } 14. Ne4 { Retreating } 14... b6 15. O-O-O a5 16. Qf4 { Improving to a more active square } { [%cal Gf4e5] } 16... Ba6 17. Bxa6 Rxa6 18. Rd2 { Prepare to double rooks on the d-file to bring more pieces to execute an attack on black's king } 18... Nf5 19. Rhd1 Rd8? 20. Nf6 Raa8 (20... Nxf6 21. exf6+ Qxf6 22. Rxd8) 21. Rxd7 Rxd7 22. Rxd7 Qb4 23. Qxb4 axb4 24. Ng5 { Bringing the final piece into the attack } 24... Nh6 25. Nxe6+ { Black resign } { [%cal Gd7g7] } *


