1. e4 c5 2. d4 cxd4 3. Qxd4? Nc6 4. Qe3 Nf6 5. h3 d5 { With the idea of opening up the centre to exploit the fact the white's queen is in the centre of the board and also opening up the diagonal to develop the light square bishop. } 6. Bd3 e5 { Control some more of the centre and again open up the diagonal for the other bishop } 7. Nf3 Be7 (7... d4? { Closing up the centre would give white time to develop and white don't have to worry about queen being attack as it can sit comfortably on e2 } 8. Qe2) 8. O-O (8. exd5 Nxd5) 8... O-O 9. Qd2?? { (Perhaps mouse slipped?) } 9... dxe4 { [%cal Ge4d3,Ge4f3,Gf6e4] } 10. Bb5 exf3 { Winning a piece and ruining's white's pawn structure } 11. gxf3 Nd4 { Close the avenue of negotiation between the queen, so that black can use his queen to start an attack later on. } { [%cal Gd2d8,Gd4f3,Gd4b5] } 12. Bd3?? Nxf3+ { White resign } { [%cal Gf3g1,Gf3d2] } *


