1. e4 b6 2. d4 Bb7 3. Nc3 g6 4. h4 { Planning shove the pawn down black's throat. } { [%cal Gh4h5,Gh5h6] } 4... Bg7 5. h5 e6 6. h6 Bf8 7. Nf3 Be7 8. e5 d5 9. exd6 { Keeping the centre open } 9... cxd6 10. d5 e5 11. Bb5+ Nd7 { Planning to go the the c6 outpost } { [%csl Gc6] } 12. Bc6 Bxc6 13. dxc6 Nb8 14. Qd5 { Again just utilizing the weakness left behind by black } 14... Qc7 15. Nb5 Qxc6 16. Nc7+ Qxc7 17. Qxa8 Nf6 18. Bg5 O-O 19. Bxf6 Bxf6 20. Qd5 Qc6 21. O-O-O Qxd5 22. Rxd5 Be7 23. Nd2 { Prepare to attack the weak pawn on d6 } { [%cal Gd2e4,Ge4d6] } 23... Bg5 24. Rxd6 Bxd2+ 25. Kxd2 f5 26. Rh3 { Bringing the rook into the game as piece activity is crucial in the end game. } { [%cal Gh3c3,Gc3c7] } 26... Kf7 27. Rc3 Re8 28. Rc7+ Re7 29. Rxe7+ Kxe7 30. Rxg6 { Sacrificing to promote the past pawn } 30... hxg6 31. h7 Kf7 32. h8=Q Nd7 33. Qa8 a5 34. Qc6 Ke7 35. Qxg6 f4 36. g4 fxg3 37. fxg3 Nf6 38. g4 e4 39. g5 Ke6 40. Qxf6+ Kd5 41. g6 Kc5 42. g7 Kd5 43. g8=Q+ Kc5 44. Qe5+ Kc6 45. Qgd5# *


