1. e4 c5 2. Nc3 Nc6 3. Nf3 g6 4. Bb5 Bg7 5. Bxc6 dxc6 { Breaking the principles to open up the bishop } { [%csl Gg4][%cal Gc8g4] } 6. O-O e5 { Control the centre } { [%cal Ge5d4,Gc5d4] } 7. d3 Ne7 8. h3 O-O 9. Bg5 h6 10. Bxe7 Qxe7 11. Qe2 f5 12. exf5 gxf5 13. Rae1 Re8 14. Nh2 Be6 15. f3?! { Open up the diagonal to the king } { [%cal Ga7g1] } 15... c4 { Open up the c5 square so that black can utilize the weakening of white's position } { [%csl Gc5][%cal Gc5g1,Ge7c5] } 16. dxc4 Qc5+ 17. Kh1 Bxc4 18. Qf2 Bf8 { Prepare to trade queens on black terms thus improving the bishop's position } 19. Ne2 Qxf2 20. Rxf2 Bc5 21. Rff1 Rad8 22. b3 Ba6 23. c4 b5 24. Rc1 bxc4 25. bxc4 Rd2 26. Ng3 Bc8 27. Nh5 Kf7 { [%cal Gh5f6] } 28. f4 e4 29. Ng3 Be6 30. Rfd1 e3 { [%cal Ge3d2] } 31. Re1 (31. Rxd2 exd2 32. Rd1 Bxc4 33. Rxd2 Re1+ { [%cal Gc4f1] }) 31... Rg8 { Attacking undefended piece } { [%cal Gg8g3] } 32. Nhf1 Rxa2 33. Nxe3?? Rxg3 { [%cal Gg3g2,Gg3e3] } 34. Rc2 Rxe3 35. Rxa2 Rxe1+ 36. Kh2 Re4 37. g3 Rxc4 38. Ra6 Bb6 { [%cal Ga6c6] } 39. Ra1 Rc2+ 40. Kh1 Bd5# *


