1. e4 e5 2. Nf3 d6 3. d4 exd4 4. Nxd4 Nf6 5. Nc3 Be7 6. Bc4 O-O (6... Nxe4 7. Qh5 { [%cal Gh5f7,Gc4f7] } 7... d5 8. Nxd5 O-O 9. O-O Bd6 10. Re1 Nf6 11. Nxf6+ Qxf6 12. Nb5) 7. Bb3 { Avoid fork trap } (7. Be3 Nxe4 8. Nxe4 d5 { [%cal Gd5c4,Gd5e4] }) 7... a6 8. O-O b5 { Preparing to trap white's bishop with tempo } { [%cal Gc7c5,Gc5c4] } 9. Bd5 { Avoid getting trap } { [%cal Gd5a8] } 9... Nxd5 10. Nxd5 (10. exd5 { Taking with pawn is also reasonable to secure an outpost on c6 } { [%cal Gd5c6,Gd4c6] }) 10... Bb7 11. Nf5 Bf6 12. Qg4 { Develop the queen to potentially accumulate the chances on attacking black's kingside } 12... Bxd5 13. exd5 Nd7 14. Bh6 { [%cal Gh6g7] } 14... g6 (14... Ne5 { This would had been a better move for black to prepare to shield black's kingside structure and unpinning. } { [%cal Ge5g6] } 15. Qg3 Ng6 { [%cal Gg3g6] }) 15. Bxf8 Qxf8 16. Nh6+ { Forcing a trade of knight in a tactical way } 16... Kg7?? 17. Qxd7 Kxh6 18. Rae1 { Bringing more pieces into the game } 18... Bxb2 19. Re7 Kg7 20. Qxc7 Rc8? { Tactical mistake } 21. Rxf7+ Qxf7 22. Qxc8 Qxd5 23. Qxa6 Qc5 24. Qb7+ { Prepare to centralise the queen and defend the c2 pawn with tempo } { [%csl Ge4][%cal Gb7e4,Ge4c2,Gb7g7] } 24... Kh6 25. Qe4 { [%cal Ge4c2] } 25... Be5 26. Rd1 { Bringing white's last piece into the game } 26... b4 27. g3 { Make room for the king to avoid back-rank threats } 27... Kg7 28. Kg2 { Unpinning and potentially allow f4 push (Weakens white's king) } { [%cal Gc5g1] } 28... Qa5 29. f4 { Since black's queen has moved away from white's king, they are not able to exploit the weakness created by advancing the pawn } 29... Bc3 30. Rxd6 Qc7 31. Qe6 { Prepare to support the rook on d7 if possible } { [%cal Gd6d7] } 31... Qb7+ 32. Qd5 Qxd5+ 33. Rxd5 h5 34. Kf3 Kf6 35. h3 Ke6 36. Ke4 Be1 37. g4 hxg4 38. hxg4 Bg3 39. f5+ gxf5+ 40. gxf5+ Kf6 41. Kd3 { Using the past pawn as a decoy to tie down black's king so that white can go to capture black's pawn to create another past pawn } { [%cal Gf6f5,Gd3c4,Gc4b4,Ga2a8] } 41... Be5 42. Rxe5 Kxe5 43. Kc4 Kxf5 44. Kxb4 Ke6 45. Kc5 Kd7 46. Kb6 Kc8 47. c4 Kb8 48. c5 Ka8 49. c6 Kb8 50. c7+ Kc8 51. a4 Kd7 { Black resign } *


