1. e4 e5 2. Nf3 d5 3. exd5 Bg4? 4. h3 { Ask what black wants to do with his bishop } 4... Bh5 5. Nc3 { Developing to prevent black from pushing pawn to e4 } { [%cal Gc3e4,Gc3d5] } 5... e4 6. Nxe4 Qe7 7. Qe2 { Unpinning } 7... Bxf3 8. Qxf3 Nf6 9. Bd3 Nxd5 10. O-O Qd8 11. Re1 Ne7? { Obstructing the development of the bishop and weakening the f7 pawn because black queen cannot move to defend it } { [%csl Gf7][%cal Gf8e7] } 12. Bc4 { Threatening to win the undefended pawn } { [%cal Gc4f7,Gf3f7] } 12... f6 (12... f5 13. Qxf5 Nxf5 14. Nf6# { [%cal Gc4f7,Gf6d7,Ge1e8,Gf6e8] }) 13. Qxf6 (13. Qh5+ { Force mate variation } 13... Kd7 14. Be6+ Kxe6 15. Nc5+ Kd6 16. Re6#) 13... gxf6 14. Nxf6# { [%cal Gc4f7,Gf6d7] } *


