1. d4 Nf6 2. e3 g6 3. Bd3 Bg7 4. c3 O-O 5. Nf3 d6 { Start to prepare the move e5 (King's Indian main idea) } { [%csl Ge5][%cal Gd6e5] } 6. Na3 Nc6 { [%csl Ge5][%cal Gc6e5,Gd6e5] } 7. Bd2 e5 8. dxe5 dxe5 9. Qc2 Qe7 { Prepare the move e4 } { [%cal Ge5e4] } 10. e4 Bg4 11. Be2 Rad8 12. h3 Be6 13. O-O Nh5 { Prepare the f5 pawn break } 14. Bg5 f6 15. Be3 f5 16. Ng5 Bc8 17. exf5 Bxf5 18. Qb3+ { [%cal Gb3g8,Gb3b7] } 18... Kh8 19. Qxb7 Nf4 { Intercept the defence of the knight by the bishop } { [%cal Ge3g5] } 20. Bxf4 exf4 21. Qxc6 Qxg5 22. Rad1 Bxh3 23. Rxd8 { [%cal Gg2h3,Gg5g1] } 23... Rxd8 24. Rd1 Rf8 { Retreating (Declining the trade) with the potential to supervise a pawn push. } { [%cal Gf4f3] } 25. Nb5 Be5 { Improving the bishop } { [%cal Ge5c7] } 26. Nd4 f3 27. Bxf3 Bc8 { Dropping the bishop back to pave a path for the queen to h2 } { [%cal Gg5h4,Gh4h2] } 28. Kf1 Qh4 29. Ne6 Rg8 30. Nxc7 Bxc7 31. Qxc7 Ba6+ 32. Kg1 Re8 33. Qc6 Qe7 34. Qxa6 g5 35. Qa4 Qe5 36. Rd5 Qe1+ 37. Kh2 g4 38. Qd4+ Kg8 39. Rg5+ Kf8 40. Qf6# *


