1. d4 Nf6 2. b3 g6 3. a3 Bg7 4. Bb2 O-O 5. Nd2 d6 { Preparing e5 (King's Indian main idea) } { [%cal Ge7e5] } 6. Ngf3 Nbd7 { Again preparing e5 } { [%cal Gd7e5,Gd6e5] } 7. e3 e5 8. e4 exd4 { Open up the centre because white's king is still in the centre } 9. Bxd4 Re8 10. Bd3 d5 { Winning the pinned pawn } 11. e5 Ng4 { Moving the knight to win the pawn } { [%cal Gg4e5] } 12. O-O Ngxe5 13. Re1 c5 { Chasing away white's strong bishop/forcing a trade if white captures the knight on e5. } { [%cal Gd4b2,Gd4e5] } 14. Bxe5 Nxe5 { [%cal Gg7a1] } 15. Ra2 Nxd3 { Removing white last bishop so that black will have a bishop pair against white's knight pair } 16. cxd3 Bf5 { Develop the bishop while eyeing the undefended pawn } { [%cal Gf5d3] } 17. Nf1 Rxe1 18. Qxe1?? Bxd3 19. Ng3 c4 { With the idea of creating a past pawn on the c-file since black's bishop is already controlling the c3 and c2 square } { [%cal Gg7c3,Gd3c2,Gc4c3,Gc3c2] } 20. bxc4 dxc4 21. h3 c3 22. Qc1 Rc8 { *Patient move
Bring more pieces into the game } 23. Ne1 c2 (23... Bc4 24. Rc2 Bb3 25. Re2 Qd1 { [%cal Gb3d1] } (25... c2 26. Nxc2 Qc7) 26. Qxd1 Bxd1 { [%cal Gc3c2] }) 24. Nf1 (24. Nxc2 Qc7 { [%cal Gc7c1] }) 24... Bxf1 25. Kxf1 Bh6 { Sacrificing the bishop to dislodge white's queen from c1 so that black can make a second queen } 26. Qxc2 Rxc2 27. Rxc2 Qd1 28. g3 Bd2 29. Rxd2 Qxd2 30. Nf3 Qc1+ 31. Kg2 Qxa3 32. h4 b5 33. Nd4 b4 34. Kf1 Qd3+ 35. Ne2 b3 36. Ke1 b2 37. Nf4 b1=Q# *


