1. e4 e5 2. Nf3 d6 3. d4 exd4 4. Nxd4 Be7 5. Nc3 Nf6 6. Bc4 O-O 7. Bb3 { Avoiding fork trap } { [%cal Gc3e4,Gf6e4,Gd6d5,Gd5c4,Gd5e4] } 7... Nbd7 8. O-O Ne5? 9. f4 { Chasing the knight away } 9... Ned7 10. Nf3 { Preparing a pawn break on e5 } { [%cal Gf3e5] } 10... Nc5 11. Qe1 { Moving the queen to avoid queen trade after e5 pawn break } { [%cal Ge4e5,Gd6e5,Gd8d1,Gf4e5] } 11... Bg4 12. e5 dxe5 13. fxe5 Nh5 14. Be3 { Continue with development } 14... Ne6 (14... Nxb3 { Black should had taken the bishop } 15. axb3 { [%cal Ga1d1,Gh2h3] }) 15. Rd1 Qe8 16. Nd5? { Centralising the knight } 16... c6 17. Nc3 { Retreating } 17... Bb4 18. h3 { With the idea to get rid of the pin } 18... Bxf3 19. Rxf3 Rd8 20. g4 { Attack the trapped knight } { [%csl Gf6,Gf4,Gg3] } 20... f5?? { *Tactical blunder
The pawn used to defend the knight of e6 } { [%cal Gf7e6] } 21. Rxd8 { Distract the overloaded queen from defending the knight of e6 } { [%cal Ge8e6,Ge8d8] } 21... Qxd8 22. Bxe6+ Kh8 23. gxh5 f4 24. Bxf4 Bc5+ 25. Kg2 Qe7 26. Bc4 { Prepare to build a battery targeting the h7 square } { [%cal Gc4d3,Gd3h7,Ge1e4] } 26... b5 27. Bd3 b4 28. Qe4 { [%cal Ge4h7] } 28... g6 29. Ne2 gxh5 30. Rg3 { Bringing the rook to participate in the attack } { [%cal Gg3g8] } 30... Rg8 31. Rxg8+ Kxg8 32. Ng3 { Bringing the knight into the attack } { [%cal Gg3f5] } 32... Qg7 { Threatening h4 due to white's knight being pinned } { [%cal Gh5h4,Gg7g2] } 33. Qc4+ Kh8 34. Qxc5 h4 35. Qd6 hxg3 36. Qd8+ Qg8 37. Qf6+ Qg7 38. Bh6 Kg8 39. Qxg7# *


