1. e4 c5 2. c3 d5 { Immediately strikes the centre } 3. exd5 Qxd5 4. d4 { Control the centre } 4... Nf6 5. Nf3 Bg4 6. Be2 e6 7. Na3 { Prepare to go b5 } { [%cal Ga3b5] } 7... a6 { Preventing white's knight from going d5 but weakens the b6 square } 8. Nc4 { Aiming for the b6 outpost } { [%cal Gc4b6,Gb6d5] } 8... Qd8 9. Qb3 { With the idea to try to provoke black to play b5 which weakens the pawn - It makes the pawn more vulnerable because it's more difficult to defend them with pieces when the pawns are not on its starting square. } 9... b5 10. Nce5 c4 11. Qd1 Bd6 12. Nxg4 Nxg4 13. a4 { Trying to undermine the base of the pawn chain to exploit the fact that it's overextended. } { [%cal Ga4b5] } 13... Nd7 14. Ng5 { Open up a discover attack on black's knight on g4 and also with the potential of improving the bishop on a more active square } { [%cal Ge2f3,Gf3g4,Gf3a8] } 14... Ngf6 15. Bf3 Rb8 16. axb5 axb5 17. O-O O-O 18. Re1 Qc7 { Attacking the pawn } { [%cal Gd6h2] } 19. h3 h6 20. Ne4 Nxe4 21. Bxe4 f5? { Weakens the pawn on e6 } { [%cal Gf7e6] } 22. Bf3 Rbe8 23. Ra6 { With the idea of occupying c6 square } 23... Nf6 24. Bc6 { [%cal Gc6b5,Gc6e8] } 24... Re7 25. Bxb5 Ne4 { Centralising the knight } 26. Bc6 { Trying to trade off black's centralise knight } { [%cal Gc6e4] } 26... Ref7 27. Bxe4 fxe4 28. Be3 { Defending } { [%cal Ge3f2] } 28... Bf4 { Trying to remove the defender of the f2 square } 29. Qg4 { Improving the queen to perhaps manouevre to a better square to help defend the king } 29... Bxe3 30. fxe3 Qb7 31. Rxe6 Qxb2 { [%cal Gb2f2,Gf2e1,Gf2g1] } 32. Kh2 { Avoiding fork } 32... Rf2 33. Rg6 { Black lost on time } { [%cal Gg6g7] } *


