1. d4 Nf6 2. c4 g6 3. Nc3 Bg7 4. Bg5 O-O 5. e4 d6 6. f4? { Positional mistake
White is breaking the principles of pushing to many pawns in the opening.
White us also overextending his pawns - white has a great central control with 4 pawns but he is not able to defend this many pawns at once. } 6... c5 { Striking white's centre not giving white a chance to develop and defend his central pawns. } 7. e5 cxd4 8. exf6 { tactical mistake } 8... exf6 { Now black is attacking white's bishop and knight, he is also ready to bring his rook into the open e-file } { [%cal Gf6g5,Gd4c3,Gf8e8,Ge8e1] } 9. Bxf6 Bxf6 10. Ne4 Re8 { [%cal Ge8e1] } 11. Nf3?? Rxe4+ 12. Be2 Qe7 { Quite move to accumulate more pressure in the centre towards white's king to tempolary stopping white's from castling. } 13. Qd3 (13. O-O Rxe2 14. Qxe2 Qxe2) 13... Re3 { [%cal Ge3d3] } 14. Qd2 d3 { Bringing the pawn to participate in the attack } { [%cal Gd3e2,Ge3e2] } 15. O-O dxe2 16. Rfe1 Nc6 { Continue developing to bring more pieces involve } 17. Rad1?? exd1=Q 18. Rxd1 Bg4 19. Ne1 Bxd1 20. Qxd1 Rxe1+ 21. Qxe1 Qxe1# *


