1. e4 c5 2. Bc4 Nc6 3. Nf3 e6 4. d3 d5 5. exd5 exd5 6. Bb3 Nf6 7. Qe2+ Be7 8. h3 O-O 9. Bf4 Re8 { [%cal Ge8e2] } 10. O-O Bf5 11. Qd2 { [%cal Gd2f4] } 11... Qd7 { Prepare to tear open white's kings side } { [%cal Gf5h3] } 12. Re1 Bxh3 13. gxh3 Qxh3 { [%cal Gh3f3] } 14. Qd1 { [%cal Gd1f3] } 14... Ng4 { Bringing more piece to the attack } 15. Bxd5 { [%cal Gd5f3] } 15... Nd4 { Trying to distract the knight (Unsound) } { [%cal Gf3d4,Ge7h4,Gh4f2] } 16. c3 (16. Nxd4 Bh4 { [%cal Gh4f2] } 17. Bg2 { [%cal Gg2h3,Gg1f1] } 17... Bxf2+ 18. Kf1 Rxe1+ 19. Qxe1 { [%cal Ge1f2,Gg2h3] } 19... Qxg2+ 20. Kxg2 Bxe1 21. Nf3) 16... Nf5 { Repositioning the knight to still be relevant with the attack } { [%cal Gf5h4] } 17. Ne5 Bh4 { Open up the rook to prepare a tactical trade } { [%cal Ge8e1] } 18. Bxf7+ Kh8 19. Qxg4 Qxg4+ 20. Nxg4 Rxe1+ { End of tactical trade } 21. Kg2 Rf8 22. Bd5 Ne7 { [%cal Ge7d5,Gf8f4] } 23. Bd6 { [%cal Gd6f8] } 23... Rf5 { Unpinning and preparing to move to rook to g5 pinning white's knight } { [%cal Gf5g5,Gg5g2] } 24. Bxe7 Bxe7 25. Ne3 Rg5+ 26. Kf3 Rgg1 { White lose on time } { [%cal Ge1a1] } *


