1. e4 d5 2. exd5 Qxd5 3. Nc3 Qd8 4. d4 c6 5. Nf3 b5 6. Bd3 Nf6 7. O-O e6 8. Ne5 { Centralising the knight } 8... Bb7 (8... Qxd4 { Tactical blunder } { [%cal Gd1d4] } 9. Nxf7 { Forcing black's king onto a square where white can give a check to win black's queen } 9... Kxf7 10. Bg6+ hxg6 11. Qxd4) 9. Bg5 Be7 10. Qf3 { [%cal Gf3a8,Gf3f7] } 10... O-O (10... Qxd4 11. Rfe1 { [%cal Ge1e5] } 11... O-O 12. Rad1 { [%cal Gd1d4,Ge1e5,Gd3h7,Gf3h3,Gh3h7] }) 11. Nxb5 { [%cal Gf3b7] } 11... Nd5 12. Bxe7 Qxe7 13. Nc3 Nxc3 14. bxc3 f6 15. Qh3 { Making a counter threat which is greater than the black's threat } { [%cal Gd3h7,Gh3h7] } 15... g6 (15... fxe5 16. Bxh7+ Kf7 17. Qh5+ Kf6 18. Qg6# (18. dxe5#)) 16. Ng4 Kh8 17. Bxg6 { [%cal Gh3h8] } 17... Rg8 18. Bd3 Qg7 19. Nxf6 { Winning the free pawn because black's queen is stuck defending against checkmate. White queen is also defending against checkmate } { [%cal Gg7f6,Gh3h7,Gh3g2,Gg7g2] } 19... Nd7 20. Nxh7 { [%cal Gh3h8] } 20... Rgf8 21. Nf6+ { Black resign } *


